# A diagnostic about a file that is not the one on screen.
#
# `pascalc` translates every program-component, and this compiler is three of
# them, so an error in a component is the ordinary case and not the corner.
# The filename was parsed off and thrown away: the cursor jumped to that line
# number *in whatever was open*, and the message arrived looking as though it
# had been landed on -- a wrong position in the wrong file with nothing
# saying so.
#
# Three claims here. A diagnostic naming this document still lands, which is
# the half that must not regress. One naming another file moves nothing and
# reports the diagnostic **as the compiler wrote it**, position and all,
# because a line number with no file is exactly what was wrong before. And
# the comparison is on the name the document has -- the shell compiles
# `EditName(ed)`, so that is the name a diagnostic about this file carries.
name p.pas
size 8 34
push program p(output);
push import q;
push begin
push   writeln(x)
push end.
draw
fault p.pas:4:11: error: 'x' is not declared
draw
fault q.pas:12:3: error: 'y' is not declared
draw
